{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47403-was-mummy-designed-to-be-a-one-chronicle-game","id":47403,"title":"Was mummy designed to be a one chronicle game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-12T08:27:43-08:00","id":47403,"title":"Was mummy designed to be a one chronicle game?","content":"This is regarding the game design. Was mummy designed to be a one chronicle game that the players can wrap up in a few sessions and move on? Given the nature of the descent, this sees like a default mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T13:55:33-08:00","id":47591,"title":"","content":"I don't think mummy was written as a one chronicle game. Playing only one descent could limit the active time of the mummies, but it is always possible to play over multiple different time periods, or play cultists in the downtime between the awakenings of the mummies.<br /> <br /> When playing only mummies, it depends on wether the mummies are on the clock. If they are on the clock they will succeed all descent roll after completing their objective. This would still mean at least one or two whole chronicles of activity and more if the mummy only accomplishes his objective late in his descent. Asuming four chapter stories and four story chronicles, the characters would have 35 sessions or 398 days of time.<br /> <br /> During a Sothic Turn there is no objective, so mummies may always make descent rolls to stay at high Sekhem longer. And when they hit Sekhem 1, they do not have to make automatic descent rolls anymore, so they could stay active indefinitely (unless they provoke their judges or are killed with aggravated). Using methods explained in Guildhalls of the Deathless, this low Sekhem rating can be overcome by boosting their effective Sekhem.<br /> <br /> So if you want to play a multiple year chronicle (both in character and out of character), I would either play during diffent time periods, play during a Sothic Turn or also give the players cultist/ghost characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:21:56-08:00","id":47680,"title":"","content":"I missed the part where they do not make descent roles at sekhem 1, where can I find that. The whole game seems fast and furious, you are a sekhem methuselah at 8+ for a long weekend! can use tier 3 utterances, for about a month, then keep sliding in power. Sure you can last several months at sekhem 1 or 2, but a mummy would be so weak that they incapable of using their power effectively","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:23:02-08:00","id":47732,"title":"","content":"You would be surprised how effective PCs can be while having 1 or 2 in Sekhem (or equivalent stat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:42:21-08:00","id":47788,"title":"","content":"There's a side-bar in the section on the Descent rules describing how Sothic awakenings affect the Descent.<br /> <br /> To OP, a Descent is a framework to sort of plan on how long the campaign will be. If you're running Mage, for example, you still break your sessions up into a variety of stories, and you do the same for Mummy. Like someone said, during a Sothic turn you can just hang out at Sekhem 1, but even then Sekhem 1 lasts &quot;one chronicle&quot; so you can justify any campaign length that you and your players need to tell the story. There's just a sort of finish line at the end of the tunnel.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, what if you don't finish the story but their Descent ends?&quot; you might ask. That's not a problem; that can be an engaging problem! What happens when your arch-nemesis has stolen a 3,000 year old relic and is going to use it to harvest the souls of your cultists, but you just died for the final time? Well, you wake up for your next Descent and have to pick up the pieces! It's not a set-back - it's conflict, and conflict is a good story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T22:33:38-08:00","id":47937,"title":"","content":"It can take a long time for a Descent to end, especially at the lower Sekhem level. As per the rules, it takes &quot;a chronicle&quot; (an entire chronicle!) to go from Sekhem 1 to 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T19:45:44-08:00","id":48666,"title":"","content":"Well it's definitely the easiest game to play in one chronicle. But...<br /> <br /> I started to really think about this question and I kind of realized something. A mummy is actually going to be a lot more active than the book implies. We live in a very active world where you can get to the other side of the globe in a matter of hours. A mummy, a mostly sedentary creature, for the first time is able to see the world without expanding so many resources and time. We don't live in a world where all you're ever going to see is your small town of 300 people and only talk to those three people you actually like. We have the internet, we're connected to everything. Because of this it's wouldn't be all that hard to imagine a cult being much more active than in the past, making deals with people in another continent or exploring multiple cities for relics. We're also so much more connected and things move so much faster, the cult will probably need a mummy now more than ever. Before a mummy would probably be awoken every couple decades for one reason or another. But now a mummy can do so much more with all the resources they've amassed. And that's also something that can be explored in a chronicle, how does the mummy adapt to this new world. Also because of this, mummies will have more time than ever to devote to personal exploration and increasing memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T20:41:52-08:00","id":48692,"title":"","content":"Also, for as much as the judges and the nature of the descent actively discourage you from trying to stick around in the world for personal reasons, the game also encourages you to start recovering your memories. A mummy who is in the process of recovering their memory and becoming more human (and possibly pursuing apotheosis) will tend to try to bend the rules and get as much time to pursue that goal as possible. While the judges and mummy society tend to frown on mummies who do stuff like ordering their cult to resurrect them for a trivial purpose as soon as possible after the end of their last descent...that's exactly the sort of rule-break-y thing that such a mummy would do (and hope no one notices). And since mummy society is very &quot;beg forgiveness, don't ask permission&quot; and they don't make a habit of checking in on each other for rule-breaking (they are all busy people with shit to do), it's the sort of thing you could feasibly get away with.<br /> <br /> In other words, the mummy who is only summoned up by their cult twice a century for tasks of Great Import is probably a great example of <i>most</i> mummies, the ones who are still good little servants. The PCs are probably not most mummies, or if they are they probably won't be for very long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 01-13-2014, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T08:59:19-08:00","id":51646,"title":"","content":"Here is my take,<br /> <br /> The mummy book was pretty vague about how often a mummy can be awoken. I got the impression that once every few generations was the average. Sure, a mummy can be awoken more often, but this might have an expense in Sekhem or other supernatural power. I got the impression that a wise cult does not awaken their mummy too much. After all, there must be some reason that mummies are not permanently awake as cults continuously restart their descents. Again, the book was not too clear about this.<br /> <br /> Now...a mummy that has started his descent has a clock ticking. He/she might stay awake for a long time, but it would be at a substantially weaker sekhem 1 or 2. Another thing, if the mummy player tries to stay awake longer, the mummy will need to do illegal things. What I mean by illegal would be, not doing what your Judge wants you to do, getting more memory, or cannibalizing Sekhem. All of these things are a big no no in mummy. If you want to say awake the longest you would need to reset your descent at Sekhem 1, 2 or 3 to get the most bang for your buck, which, ironically, is when you are the weakest.<br /> <br /> I can see a parallel with Demon the Descent, be a good angel that is a slave or a free demon that is weak. A mummy that extends his life and get more memory and do his thing is probably going to draw the wrath of the judges. The judges will probably send a more loyal mummy with Sekhem 10 to crush the offending mummy and send him back to Duat for punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T09:57:59-08:00","id":51678,"title":"","content":"Actually, it is very straightforward how often Mummies can be expected to wake up. Pg. 214, in the sidebar 'How Deep the Well'. It is in the ST Handbook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T11:00:14-08:00","id":51709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47403-was-mummy-designed-to-be-a-one-chronicle-game?p=51678#post51678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it is very straightforward how often Mummies can be expected to wake up. Pg. 214, in the sidebar 'How Deep the Well'. It is in the ST Handbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really answer how often cults <i>do</i> wake their Mummies, though. I mean, by the default rules, a cult with a Mummy with a one-dot centering Relic could keep their patron active indefinitely, but that's clearly not the intent of the game, which describes long periods of inactivity.<br /> <br /> However, there IS a good reason for a Mummy to not want to be summoned too often - Memory. At Memory 3, which most Mummies tend to return to unless they make an effort to stay above or below it, you remember Irem (or things you heard about Irem; it's hard to keep them separate) and your <i>prior Descent</i>. (*) The more often you get woken, the more you lose, especially since you lose a dot of Memory at the end of every Descent. You have to get up to Memory 5 before you can even get rough knowledge of your other Descents, and keeping that relies on regularly re-purchasing Memory 6+. <i>Most Mummies</i> aren't going to bother, and so are going to want to make sure that their cult summons them only when opportune - when they're necessary, or when there's the opportunity to earn a lot of Descent resets. (**) This is even true of Mummies who are interested in building up their Memory, as increasing your Memory prompts a Descent roll, so it's important that they arrange their agenda and circumstances to earn a lot of resets.<br /> <br /> (*) - I exclude Descents where the Arisen completes a brief objective and returns to Duat without going through a full Descent from this <i>and</i> the Memory loss. I assume that many tomb violations and cult ceremonies are handled quickly and easily, with the Mummy returning to death before they're finished &quot;booting up&quot; or soon after, and thus not incurring either hit.<br /> <br /> (**) - In addition to those listed, I presume that &quot;secure vessels with the intent of returning them to Duat&quot; is within <i>every</i> Judge's agenda, and so always earns a reset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T11:02:04-08:00","id":51711,"title":"","content":"I remember that part. I wonder though, if it was possible to resurrect mummies so frequently, why do they not do it more often? Another paragraph at the beginning states that mummies are usually resurrected much more infrequently. I got the impression that cults can resurrect every few months or so, but there are some restrictions on why they do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T11:32:06-08:00","id":51737,"title":"","content":"Because the cultists don't want to interact with the mummy that floods their minds with Sybaris every time they wake it up, or because the mummy forbade it except in certain circumstances, or they're just frugal about their occult resources like that, or any number of reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T11:53:06-08:00","id":51755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47403-was-mummy-designed-to-be-a-one-chronicle-game?p=51646#post51646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see a parallel with Demon the Descent, be a good angel that is a slave or a free demon that is weak. A mummy that extends his life and get more memory and do his thing is probably going to draw the wrath of the judges. The judges will probably send a more loyal mummy with Sekhem 10 to crush the offending mummy and send him back to Duat for punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be overestimating how much awareness the judges have of a mummy's activities, and how much direct influence they have. As it stands, the judges can't wake a mummy, and the only way they can give a mummy &quot;orders&quot; is by giving said mummy resets when it happens to be pursuing the thing they want pursued. &quot;There's a mummy in cairo that is getting funny ideas, I need you to book a flight and go stomp on his head&quot; is probably a bit beyond them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T01:30:39-08:00","id":52220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47403-was-mummy-designed-to-be-a-one-chronicle-game?p=51755#post51755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you may be overestimating how much awareness the judges have of a mummy's activities, and how much direct influence they have. As it stands, the judges can't wake a mummy, and the only way they can give a mummy &quot;orders&quot; is by giving said mummy resets when it happens to be pursuing the thing they want pursued. &quot;There's a mummy in cairo that is getting funny ideas, I need you to book a flight and go stomp on his head&quot; is probably a bit beyond them.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it's likey the Maa-Kep and Su-Menent already have their eyes on such a Mummy, and are very eager and willing to earn a reset by mulching a potential heretic. In a game session yesterday, one of my PCs decided to go on a full anti Irem rant because he didn't have much memory anymore, and took a hit to his Sekhem just by CONSIDERING the idea that the Judges were lying. Granted, he wasn't politely hinting, he was getting pretty.. &quot;blasphemous&quot;. It was to a cultist of another Mummy, thankfully (Otherwise theyd've both suffered a Sekhem hit). But youd be amazed at how effective the ancient Iremite technology of Carrot and Stick works in the right context. The player of the Cultist (Who was a Mummy's off character) is now starting to wonder about how much the Judges care, or how much this cultist trusts them watching his mummy crush wither and deage before his very eyes for speaking against the Judges.<br /> <br /> The way I began to think of it.. I think the default is the opposite of what we assume. We assume that MOST cults are smart, and don't wake up their Mummy often.. so that they have few memories, little real impact in the world or place in it, but are SMARTLY conserving said memory. But that isn't the case. The standard PC mummy is at Memory 3 for a reason--its the lowest you can get without truly abandoning your humanity. Judging from the sidebar and all, and how often most functional groups tend towards &quot;everyone is a mummy&quot; or &quot;I'm trying to be awake most of the time so I can really do cool stuff&quot;.. and how hard and weird things have become in the last century or so, once the first few Sothic Mummies woke up, and the Egyptology boom hit.. I think most Mummies have been overused, by the Judges and their Cults. I imagine MOST of a Mummy's life is a neverending Memory 3 cycle, with occasional spikes.. mostly just remembering your last life, and thus have Playable Continuity.. but little of the past. Youre just a mummy right now, with occasional bits of flavor from the past.<br /> <br /> At default level of Memory, most mummies wouldn't even remember the countless petty lifetimes they've lived. They still can't even remember the major ones, yet. But by endgame, memory 8 and 9? You may find yourself exploring a far MORE coherent and active existence than we think. The developers said Mummies experience life as a flash of hazy images, scattered across time, with little continuity. But if a Mummy at memory 3 just.. kept going, his older lives would disappear from his mind. It isn't that they didn't LIVE all this time.. its just that their Memory of it is gone.<br /> <br /> But the intended route of the PCs is to learn how to master their Curse, not be enslaved by it. Get frugal. Figure out how to not piss off the judges, but also not earn a quick ticket back home to Duat.. how to explore himself, while also keeping the Judges and other Mummies happy. They learn to play the game.. and suddenly, a &quot;starter&quot; mummy becomes a SMARTER mummy.. ones that don't just burn through their thousands of years worth of XP in a death cycle Memory game. Ones that learn to grow, like living people do. And indeed, some begin to see a way out, off in the distance.. if theyre willing to give up the gifts that came with their Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 01-18-2014, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:24:19-08:00","id":52717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47403-was-mummy-designed-to-be-a-one-chronicle-game?p=52220#post52220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but it's likey the Maa-Kep and Su-Menent already have their eyes on such a Mummy, and are very eager and willing to earn a reset by mulching a potential heretic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why it makes sense to me that mummies who are starting to entertain heretical thoughts would start withdrawing more and more from mummy society. Because of the way their society is structured, it's almost impossible to differentiate &quot;intentionally withdrawing&quot; from &quot;has been busy/not awake&quot;, so it's pretty difficult for the secret police to keep tabs on every potential heretic unless those heretics are stupid enough to keep checking in to update everyone on their heresy. Basically, they built a huge security flaw into their culture, in that, if they don't see you then as far as they're concerned you're not doing anything. It is absurdly easy to drop off of the radar as a mummy without anyone even realizing that's weird.<br /> <br /> None of which is to say that you <i>can't</i> get caught. Accidentally running into a Maa-kep while you're pursuing some heretical piece of wisdom, and having that Maa-kep suddenly realize that she earns a reset every time she fucks with you...is the stuff stories are made of. I just think there should be a difference between &quot;you could get caught&quot; and &quot;you will definitely get caught, you would be stupid to even attempt this&quot;<br /> <br /> After all, it's implied that The Heretic (capital letters!) was a high-ranking scribe before he went AWOL. I'd set my bets on him being a Guildmaster of his Nome, wherever that was. If even a guildmaster can fall off the radar long enough to achieve Apotheosis, it's doable for everyone else.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I basically agree about how <i>most</i> mummies have historically gotten through their unlives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T10:22:06-08:00","id":54743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47403-was-mummy-designed-to-be-a-one-chronicle-game?p=52717#post52717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why it makes sense to me that mummies who are starting to entertain heretical thoughts would start withdrawing more and more from mummy society. Because of the way their society is structured, it's almost impossible to differentiate &quot;intentionally withdrawing&quot; from &quot;has been busy/not awake&quot;, so it's pretty difficult for the secret police to keep tabs on every potential heretic unless those heretics are stupid enough to keep checking in to update everyone on their heresy. Basically, they built a huge security flaw into their culture, in that, if they don't see you then as far as they're concerned you're not doing anything. It is absurdly easy to drop off of the radar as a mummy without anyone even realizing that's weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guildhalls also has a bunch of <i>really great</i> examples of Arisen heresy in action. I think there's three or four NPCs in there who are totally off the reservation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T15:55:16-08:00","id":68683,"title":"","content":"Reading the part based on the Call, I was able to figure about the gist of the mechanics of a call. When a cult decides to awaken a mummy, they need a relic that belonged to the mummy, with a bunch of vestiges that would help the call along. The key point being that <i>the relic needed to have belonged to the mummy, probably during his or her breathing days. </i>It then goes on to say, that if they do not have a relic that a mummy had, which is a semi regular occurrence, then they can sacrifice a foreign relic to make the call. However, they said that sacrificing a relic to wake a mummy makes about as much sense as burning down a house to fix a roach problem.<br /> <br /> So, that would indicate to me that...only mummies who posses relics can be awoken on a constant basis of one call after another. If the cult does not have a relic that belonged to the mummy, then they need to get hold of one and sacrifice it to make a call. Given the rarity of relics, this would be a desperate measure.<br /> <br /> In addition, every time a mummy gets awoken their memory drops by one. So... I wonder if too many awakenings in a short period would make for a ravenous beast.<br /> <br /> Another point. To really be awoken on a regular basis, a mummy would need to have made an investment in both relic, and cult. I noticed that, in the 5 pre generated mummies that were given in the supplement, 3 had a cult, one had a relic, and one had a vestige, but not one of them had both a cult and a relic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T17:43:55-08:00","id":68726,"title":"","content":"Here is my interpretation of the Call. Amon-tep is a member of the Maa-Kep. During his days in the Egyptian empire, he was an overseer and his prized possession was a beer mug which he would use to drink with his buddies after a hard day of whipping slaves to build the pyramids. The Egyptian empire was one of the greatest civilizations on Earth due the invention of beer (actually, the term those days was mead). His greatest joy was to gather with his friends and drink beer near the Nile.<br /> <br /> Eventually, after he became a mummy, this beer mug became a relic. It was infused with Sekhem and had supernatural power. If someone held it, it would magically fill with the same mead that was invented during the Egyptian empire (or, if it was cursed, would fill with Molson Canadian). It was his prized possession and his cult would use it to awaken him during the centuries. Every time he awoke, he could remember drinking beer in the hot sun overlooking the Nile. Sometimes, his cult would need to issue multiple Calls. Not often, but there was sometimes an emergency situation. The relic would refresh with energy because it was his beer mug.<br /> <br /> Then, one day he awakens and the beer mug was\u2026.GONE! When he asked the high priest what happened the priest responded that, during his sleep, another mummy stole his relic and stole the Sekhem so that he could stay awake for a few more weeks. In a furious rage, Amon-tep sought out the offending mummy. Unfortunately, the mummy was asleep, but at least Amon-tep made sure that the cult of the interloper was slaughtered to a man. That is what you get for taking his beer mug.<br /> <br /> Now, every time his cult tries to awaken him, they need to sacrifice a relic or vestige to do it. The cult was able to steal a relic quill for a future awakening\u2026but it is not the same! That was his beer mug! Nothing in the world will ever replace it and now it is gone forever! The quill will work for one Call and then it will be gone forever. <br /> <br /> Somewhere out there, a mummy scribe of the Sesha-Hebsu guild is brooding. Someone stole his quill that his cult has awoken him with for centuries. He remembers drawing rude and obscene pictures on papyrus which were highly amusing to the other scribes, and now some bastard has stolen it. He will find that mummy and make him pay for stealing his prized possession and probably wasting the Sekhem. <br /> <br /> There will be blood, things were going to get really ugly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T09:21:30-08:00","id":69129,"title":"","content":"DaveB has an actual play podcast of his Mummy game, which is as of now in its 3rd story and second time period. Might help you get an idea for how longer mummy chronicles could be done.<br /> You can find it here: <a href=\"http://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/2013/07/02/mummy-the-curse-destroyer-of-worlds-episode-1/\" target=\"_blank\">http://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com...lds-episode-1/</a><br /> A 'book club' that summarizes the podcasts can be found <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?714475-Mummy-the-Curse-Destroyer-of-Worlds-(AP-Podcast-Book-Club-)\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:38:21-08:00","id":70741,"title":"","content":"Its a little strange, though, that the example the Core gives of a renewable relic that can be used for the Call was the Centering Relic--which explicitly does NOT have to have been yours in Irem. This is implied by the &quot;exception&quot; to lifeweb rules that allow an Arisen to keep any vessel he personally owned in life. Thus, using these ideas together, my interpretation that any Relic that would function in the Lifeweb can also be used for the Call, even if he didn't own it himself until the Judges and his duty took it into his tomb to center it, or a creation of the shaniatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}